1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,920
alRato. Snap the board. Stay in class. Understand it al
rato.

2
00:00:05,025 --> 00:00:11,459
Every class ends the same way: the board fills up, the
phones come out, and the photo lands in a camera roll.

3
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:15,680
alRato turns each photo into an organized note. These two
are sample notes that ship with the app.

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:20,720
A generated whiteboard stands in for a real photo. It goes
through the same pipeline a photo would.

5
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,130
The app asks before any cloud model is used. Only the
student can agree to it.

6
00:00:26,522 --> 00:00:35,080
Reading the board runs on the cloud model. The wait is cut;
the receipts are real.

7
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:43,391
Reading handwriting prefers the cloud. The receipt shows the
route the SDK actually took.

8
00:00:43,491 --> 00:00:57,160
This note is an exercise, so it gets a hint ladder. It
teaches instead of answering.

9
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:08,233
It connects the exercise to a note you already have. It
matches what the exercise needs against what older notes
teach, so the weighted average note appears even though the
words differ.

10
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:17,289
Practice turns the note into a question you answer from
memory, then check yourself.

11
00:01:17,389 --> 00:01:22,938
The review is scheduled, and it comes back over the
following days. Recall and spacing are among the
best-supported study techniques.

12
00:01:23,038 --> 00:01:33,122
Now the connection drops. A new photo is saved at once and
waits. When the network returns, alRato finishes the note by
itself.

13
00:01:33,222 --> 00:01:38,031
Back online, the note finishes by itself, with no taps.

14
00:01:38,131 --> 00:01:41,819
A handwritten board stands in for a real photo. This one is
marked private before it is saved.

15
00:01:41,919 --> 00:01:48,846
Mark a note private and it never leaves this device. This
computer has no local model, so the note waits instead of
going to the cloud.

16
00:01:48,946 --> 00:01:55,886
On a computer with Gemini Nano, the same hints run locally.
This recording was made on a computer without it, so every
answer here came from the cloud model.

17
00:01:55,986 --> 00:02:01,908
Snap it now. Understand it al rato. Open source (Apache-2.0)
· Built with Firebase AI Logic · alrato-e3564.web.app
